    <briefdescription>
<para>DMN 1.5 decision table evaluator. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Supports loading decision tables from JSON (native format) or from a simplified DMN XML subset. Evaluates decision tables against an input context using the FEEL subset supported by this implementation.</para>
<para>FEEL subset supported:<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>Number comparisons: <computeroutput>&gt;5</computeroutput>, <computeroutput>&gt;=5</computeroutput>, <computeroutput>&lt;5</computeroutput>, <computeroutput>&lt;=5</computeroutput>, <computeroutput>=5</computeroutput>, <computeroutput>!=5</computeroutput> </para>
</listitem><listitem><para>String equality: <computeroutput>&quot;value&quot;</computeroutput> </para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Range: <computeroutput></computeroutput>[a..b], <computeroutput></computeroutput>(a..b], <computeroutput></computeroutput>[a..b), <computeroutput></computeroutput>(a..b)</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Any / wildcard: <computeroutput>-</computeroutput> (matches anything)</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Null check: <computeroutput>null</computeroutput>, <computeroutput>not(null)</computeroutput> </para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Boolean: <computeroutput>true</computeroutput>, <computeroutput>false</computeroutput> </para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
<para>Usage: <programlisting><codeline><highlight class="normal"><ref refid="classthemis_1_1process_1_1_dmn_evaluator_1a508dd7d73ab5d4548246b8eaad86fa4e" kindref="member">DmnEvaluator</ref><sp/>eval;</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">eval.loadFromJson(dmn_table_json);</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight><highlight class="keyword">auto</highlight><highlight class="normal"><sp/>result<sp/>=<sp/>eval.evaluate(</highlight><highlight class="stringliteral">&quot;risk_assessment&quot;</highlight><highlight class="normal">,<sp/>{{</highlight><highlight class="stringliteral">&quot;amount&quot;</highlight><highlight class="normal">,<sp/>5000},<sp/>{</highlight><highlight class="stringliteral">&quot;type&quot;</highlight><highlight class="normal">,<sp/></highlight><highlight class="stringliteral">&quot;credit&quot;</highlight><highlight class="normal">}});</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight><highlight class="comment">//<sp/>result[&quot;risk_level&quot;]<sp/>==<sp/>&quot;HIGH&quot;</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting> </para>
    </detaileddescription>
